      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nA big amount of grammar mistakes for a scientific expose make it very unprofessional. I did not mark all of your mistakes, but the sheer amount of little mistakes makes it hard to read. If you have troubles finding them yourself, let someone else proofread or use grammar tools online (and mention them in case)."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The theoretical framework should consist of some principles or theories that your further research is based on. What you mentioned in the section is no theoretical framework to me. As this section is not always obvious for all kinds of theses, it can also be very technical - either in the direction of explaining LLMs/GenAI, and how you would train/finetune/apply it, or in the direction of how you want to conduct your interviews."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "A good SOTA section combines different material, and presents a relevant overview over related papers or related methodologies. You mention some papers, but they are very general ([4],[6]) or not explained enough in detail ([8]). If you combine them well, provide enough detail and show their limitations, it is much easier to tell a story and justify your research"
  },
  {
